_pass":true,"reasons":["passes the trend template (7/7)","RS 99","Chemicals & Petrochemicals is a leading sector"],"pinned":true,"pin_note":"Ranked 5th of 8 - the purest H-acid exposure in the cluster and the ONLY name with a second, independent lever: it is itself the applicant in a live DGTR anti-dumping investigation into Beta Naphthol from China. Trades at 1.07x book, barely above the value of eight plants in a business where global capacity is the binding constraint. What holds it back: its Dye Intermediates segment actually FELL 4% in Q1 while margin compressed 11.66% -> 9.72%, and it carries ESM Stage I - a 100% margin requirement, so effectively no MTF. Q2 FY27 (around November) is the decisive test: it is the first quarter that contains the H-acid move at all.","rank":108},{"code":"BHAGERIA","name":"Bhageria Indust.","sector":"Chemicals & Petrochemicals","industry":"Dyes And Pigments","band":"Micro","mcap":1302,"price":303.7,"score":5.0,"rs":91,"sector_rs":61,"r1d":-0.91,"r1w":-4.81,"from_52wh":-12.45,"new_high":false,"trend":"7/7","trend_pass":true,"reasons":["passes the trend template (7/7)","RS 91","Chemicals & Petrochemicals is a leading sector"],"pinned":true,"pin_note":"Ranked 2nd of 8. Seven consecutive quarters of sequential revenue growth, margin +255bps - and it pre-dates the H-acid squeeze, so the thesis is optionality rather than the whole case. Watching Q2 FY27 (around November) for the eighth quarter with H-acid realisations in the numbers.","rank":143},{"code":"IGPL","name":"I G Petrochems","sector":"Chemicals & Petrochemicals","industry":"Commodity Chemicals","band":"Micro","mcap":1653,"price":533.3,"score":3.0,"rs":74,"sector_rs":61,"r1d":1.53,"r1w":-4.29,"from_52wh":-9.61,"new_high":false,"trend":"7/7","trend_pass":true,"reasons":["passes the trend template (7/7)","Chemicals & Petrochemicals is a leading sector"],"pinned":true,"pin_note":"Ranked 4th of 8, just 0.2 behind Foseco - effectively tied for third, and the comparative note says to